{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Working Hard", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Oops! I Made a Mistake.", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 10, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 9, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": " Analyze issues relating to different topics and their solution in written and spoken situations according to work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to pull your weight", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to do your part", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: According to some of the other copy editors, you have not really been pulling your weight. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le09ob10aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to talk about jobs, professions and careers.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to infer", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to \u200bform an \u200bopinion or \u200bguess that something is \u200btrue because of the \u200binformation that you have", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I infer from that response that it could have been better.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le09ob10aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to muddle up", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to make a mess of", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: In the words of the rep, you really \u201cmuddled it up.\u201d", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le09ob10aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to pitch in", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to \u200bstart to do something as \u200bpart of a \u200bgroup, \u200bespecially something \u200bhelpful", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The team says that you haven't pitched in as much as you could have. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le09ob10aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "hugely", "type": "name"}, {"content": "extremely", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: That paper can't be returned, and it is hugely expensive.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le09ob10aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "performance", "type": "name"}, {"content": "how well a \u200bperson, \u200bmachine, etc. does a \u200bpiece of \u200bwork or an \u200bactivity", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We need to talk about your performance this week.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le09ob10aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to get something straight ", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to understand correctly or make something clear", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: She suggested that you get the order straight before you make the call.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le09ob10aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Quoting, Reporting and Interpreting", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You use a number of different phrases or sentence structures to talk about what other people have said or written.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": " Look at the chart for an outline of some phrases you can use to quote, report or interpret others' speech.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Phrase\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" I infer from \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" interpret what you read or hear\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> I infer from that response that it could have been better.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" According to\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" refer directly to what someone said or wrote\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">According to some of the other copy editors, you have not really been pulling your weight. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" ____ says ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" refer directly to what someone said or wrote\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">The team says that you haven't contributed as much as you could have. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Your comments imply ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" interpret what you read or hear\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Your comments imply that I made a mistake, but I ordered what you told me to order.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" In the words of ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" refer directly to what someone said or wrote\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">In the words of the rep, you really \u201cmuddled it up.\u201d </span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Reported Structures: Types of Clauses", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You use different types of clauses when you report what you have heard or read.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can use three types of clauses:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "1. <span class=\"underline\">That-clauses</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use that-clauses to <span class=\"strong\">report statements</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">He claimed <span class=\"strong\">that I had done a good job</span>.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "2. <span class=\"underline\">Wh-clauses</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use wh-clauses to <span class=\"strong\">report questions with wh-words</span> (why, when, how etc.)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Mr. Brody asked me <span class=\"strong\">how this mistake could have been made</span>.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "3. <span class=\"underline\">If-clauses</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use if-clauses to <span class=\"strong\">report yes/no questions</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Mr. Brody called me to check <span class=\"strong\">if you were settling in</span>.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "She reported that you were very unclear on the phone and she had a hard time understanding you.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "She suggested that you get the order straight before you make the call.", "type": "example"}]}, {"content": "engenn10le09ob10re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "On a piece of paper, write down five events that made your week a very bad one at work or school. (You can invent those events, or you can use Adam's bad week).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Exchange lists of mistakes with a partner.  ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For each of your partner's mistakes, write down a few sentences describing what you would do to fix the mistakes.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read the mistakes and your solutions to your class or a group.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I write a list of possible mistakes.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write solutions to my partner's mistakes.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I read the mistakes and solutions aloud to a group.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "type": "WLC", 